# React standards

Based on react.dev Rules of React and Next.js App Router conventions.

## Components
- Functional components only; no class components.
- Keep components pure: same props/state → same UI; no side effects during render.
- One main component per file; name matches filename (`HeroSearchCta.tsx`).
- Prefer composition over prop drilling and giant prop bags.
- Colocate small helpers next to the component; extract shared UI into `src/components/`.

## Hooks & state
- Follow Rules of Hooks (top level only, stable dependency arrays).
- Don't put derived values in state — compute during render.
- Don't sync state with Effects when you can derive or handle in the event.
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks (`useXxx`) when used twice or the component is hard to read.
- Avoid `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default; add only for measured cost or required referential stability.

## Effects & data
- Effects are for syncing with an external system, not for "reacting to state changes".
- Prefer Server Components / route `page.tsx` data loading when possible; mark client islands with `"use client"` only when needed (events, browser APIs, local state).
- Don't fetch in Effects if a Server Component, route handler, or existing loader already covers it.

## TypeScript & props
- Type props explicitly; avoid `any`. Prefer narrow unions over stringly types.
- Use `type` for props/unions unless extending an interface is clearer.
- Event handlers: name `handle*` inside components, `on*` in props.

## JSX & a11y
- Use semantic HTML; interactive elements must be keyboard-accessible.
- Images: prefer `next/image` with meaningful `alt` (empty alt only for decorative).
- Lists need stable `key`s (id, not array index unless static/order-fixed).

## Project fit (tenerifly)
- Match existing patterns: Tailwind utility classes, Mantine where already used, locale via `useTranslation` / `createLocaleLink`.
- Don't introduce new UI libraries or state managers without an explicit ask.
- Keep changes focused; no drive-by refactors of unrelated files.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — derived state + Effect
const [fullName, setFullName] = useState("");
useEffect(() => setFullName(`${first} ${last}`), [first, last]);

// ✅ GOOD — derive during render
const fullName = `${first} ${last}`;
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — client fetch when server can load
"use client";
useEffect(() => { fetch("/api/items").then(...) }, []);

// ✅ GOOD — Server Component loads; client only for interaction
// page.tsx (server) fetches; ClientWidget receives props
```
